## 1. What Is Network Reconnaissance?

Network reconnaissance is the process of gathering information about systems, services, ports, and network structure.

Port scanning is one technique used to discover which ports are open, closed, or filtered.

### Common Types of Scanning

| Scan type | Description |
|---|---|
| TCP Connect scan | Attempts to establish a complete TCP connection |
| SYN scan | Uses TCP SYN packets to probe ports without completing a normal connection |
| UDP scan | Sends UDP probes to identify available UDP services |
| Horizontal scan | Probes the same port across multiple hosts |
| Vertical scan | Probes multiple ports on a single host |

Reconnaissance can be legitimate, such as an administrator auditing a server, or suspicious when unauthorised.

