## 12. SOC Interview Questions

**Q1. What is port scanning?**

A technique for probing ports on a host to determine which services may be available.

**Q2. What is the difference between a vertical and horizontal scan?**

A vertical scan probes multiple ports on one host; a horizontal scan probes the same port across multiple hosts.

**Q3. Does a TCP SYN packet prove port scanning?**

No. SYN packets are part of normal TCP connection establishment. Repeated probes across many ports or hosts may provide stronger evidence.

**Q4. What does a TCP RST indicate?**

A TCP reset abruptly rejects or terminates a connection. In a scan, RST responses can indicate closed ports, depending on the context.

**Q5. What should an L1 SOC analyst do after identifying possible reconnaissance?**

Validate the source, destination, time window, and expected activity; collect evidence; assess severity; and escalate according to organisational policy.

